  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 1208 AM CDT Fri Sep 25 2026\n\nWeekend conditions: Shortwave energy will continue to bring \nisolated to scattered showers and possibly some thunderstorms \nthrough the weekend, with the greatest chances of 50-70% being \nwest of Highway 65 Saturday night. Elsewhere, chances range from\n10-40% (lowest over south-central Missouri). NBM 48 hour QPF \nprobabilities for >= 0.1\" ranges from < 15% over south-central \nMO to 40% long I-44 to 60-80% over southeast KS and west-central\nMO. Some areas may stay dry. High temperatures in the mid 70s \nto mid 80s are expected.\n\nNext system Tuesday into the middle of next week: Continuing to\nsee models shift in how they handle a system that may impact the\narea. Models are now showing a deeper system, generally closing\nthat off over the SW CONUS while merging with remnants of\nHurricane Polo. SW closed lows are notoriously poorly handled by\nmodels, which is made even worse by merging with the Hurricane.\nThis leads to significant differences in timing, strength,\ntrack, and structure throughout the model spectrum. This leads\nto low confidence. Will continue monitoring for heavy rainfall\nand severe threats with this system, both of which are low at\nthis time. Confidence may not increase into early next week as\nthe system becomes more mature.",
